and R. Balescu, Physica 25, 281, 302 (1959) and references given therein;"}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "22", "artid": "621", "year": 1956, "page_start": "621", "journal_title": "Physica"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Brout, R."}, {"full_name": "Prigogine, I."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "R. Brout and I. Prigogine, Physica 22, 621 (1956)."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "3", "title": {"title": "Ensemble density"}, "misc": ["is used to denote either a quantum mechanical density matrix or a classical phase space distribution function"]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "3.“Ensemble density” is used to denote either a quantum mechanical density matrix or a classical phase space distribution function."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "4", "misc": ["A kinetic equation is called Markoffian if it involves properties of an ensemble density only at a single time"]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "4.A kinetic equation is called Markoffian if it involves properties of an ensemble density only at a single time."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "5", "publication_info": {"year": 1957}, "misc": ["Revs. Modern Phys. 29, 74"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Fano, U."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "5.U. Fano, Revs. Modern Phys. 29, 74 (1957)."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "6", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "79", "artid": "469", "year": 1950, "page_start": "469", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Lippman, B."}, {"full_name": "Schwinger, J."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "6.B. Lippman and J. Schwinger, Phys. Rev. 79, 469 (1950)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/48525"}}], "referenced_authors_bais": ["Julian.Seymour.Schwinger.1", "B.A.Lippmann.1"], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}], "author_count": 1, "first_author": {"full_name": "Zwanzig, Robert", "last_name": "Zwanzig", "first_name": "Robert", "recid": 2259374}, "control_number": 2735417, "dois": [{"source": "AIP", "value": "10.1063/1.1731409"}], "earliest_date": "1960-11-01", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Zwanzig:1960gvu"], "abstracts": [{"source": "AIP", "value": "We describe a new formulation of methods introduced in the theory of irreversibility by Van Hove and Prigogine, with the purpose of making their ideas easier to understand and to apply. The main tool in this reformulation is the use of projection operators in the Hilbert space of Gibbsian ensemble densities. Projection operators are used to separate an ensemble density into a ``relevant'' part, needed for the calculation of mean values of specified observables, and the remaining ``irrelevant'' part. The relevant part is shown to satisfy a kinetic equation which is a generalization of Van Hove's ``master equation to general order.'' Diagram summation methods are not used. The formalism is illustrated by a new derivation of the Prigogine‐Brout master equation for a classical weakly interacting system.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "AIP"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "AIP", "title": "Ensemble Method in the Theory of Irreversibility"}], "facet_author_name": ["2259374_Robert Zwanzig"], "core": false, "imprints": [{"date": "1960-11-01"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2735417", "updated": "2023-12-12T09:28:19.995881"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["J. Chem. Phys.", "J.Chem.Phys."]}, "id": "2735417", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735417?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=